sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) & Morelli et al. (2009) zebrafish Delta-Notch delayed Kuramoto phase synchrony on an advected FGF8/Wnt-graded PSM lattice: kinematic waves, Mib1-gated coupling, emergent DAPT ALD/PRP — MorphoEval overall 86.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 remediated evaluation of `2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py` (86.5/100, down from 91.3 in Pass 2). Both v2 remediation items are closed in reduced, declared form: the lattice is now an advected 24 x 12 AP x lateral delayed Kuramoto PSM under a tailbud-anchored FGF8/Wnt frequency profile with per-column period-scaled delays, producing posterior -> anterior kinematic phase waves (N_w = 1.58 vs the Law-4 analytic 1.61, anterior wavelength 2.21 S vs 2.00 S, monotone in f_A, absent for a uniform profile) that fade and recover across the DAPT pulse; and the Delta-Notch coupling is a dynamical variable kappa(t) = kappa_max u(t) g(t) with Mib1 ubiquitination kinetics and DAPT clearance (mib1-null desynchronises like early DAPT, dose sweep monotone, Mib1 restoration rescues with tau_u = 10 min). The remediation also exposed and removed Pass 2's hard-coded ALD/PRP (its 5-regime \"validation\" compared the reference JSON with itself) and an uncited instantaneous mean-field torque; ALD/PRP are now emergent (5-seed RMSE 0.22 somites, r = 0.9998) and the DAPT period lengthening is emergent in the somite count. Six Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys) back laws 1-6. The score falls because the specimen is a chick embryo mislabelled as zebrafish in Passes 1-2 and is still compared only via a fitted sinusoid, two new measurement references are model-internal, and three rate constants are calibrated to the validation data. Overall 86.5/100 (faithfulness 84.4, reproducibility 91.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/delta_notch_phase_synchrony_comparison.png: rendered output of 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py at d58a084, image/png, 1996337 B, 2436×2044 px, artifact_sha256 24bdb2e7c7c300913001ecb821a0c2953e925858f4f6af09969f9ddf45047588 (sha256 24bdb2e7c7c300913001ecb821a0c2953e925858f4f6af09969f9ddf45047588), spec_fingerprint 09e5aac12df2ce2cf18eea96b6a21a56461679db4c6b4516072331c47fa27633. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 09e5aac12df2ce2cf18eea96b6a21a56461679db4c6b4516072331c47fa27633; artifact_sha256: 24bdb2e7c7c300913001ecb821a0c2953e925858f4f6af09969f9ddf45047588; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/delta_notch_phase_synchrony/delta_notch_phase_synchrony_reference.json=209a056625b68a89..., datasets/delta_notch_phase_synchrony/scout_manifest.json=e3250a43b4bc0c22..., datasets/delta_notch_phase_synchrony/zebrafish_psm_synchrony_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) Science 317:1911-1915 & Morelli et al. (2009) HFSP J. 3:55-66 delayed Kuramoto phase-oscillator model dtheta_i/dt = omega_i + (kappa/z)*sum_j sin(theta_j(t - tau_c) - theta_i(t)) + xi_i(t), collective frequency shift Omega = omega_0 - kappa*sin(Omega*tau_c), linear stability stiffness kappa_eff = kappa*cos(Omega*tau_c) > 0 | Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007): DAPT pulse-chase Anterior Limit of Defects ALD(s_in) = s_in + ~5.5 somites (obs 5.4 +/- 0.8, 9.6 +/- 0.9, 14.4 +/- 0.9 for s_in = 0, 4, 9) and Posterior Rescue Point PRP = 14.7 +/- 1.1 after washout at s_out = 9; mib/aei/des/bea mutants desynchronise like early DAPT | Morelli et al. (2009) frequency profile omega(x) and kinematic phase waves k = (Omega - omega(x))/v travelling posterior -> anterior; Soroldoni et al. (2014) order 1-2 waves across the zebrafish PSM, waves slowing anteriorly; Herrgen et al. (2010) DAPT lengthens the segmentation period | Itoh et al. (2003): Mind bomb E3 ubiquitin ligase ubiquitinates Delta, required for Delta endocytosis and trans-activation of Notch; mib^ta52b abolishes Delta-Notch signalling; reconstructed_in_script: Transcendental collective frequency solver and 2D (tau_c, kappa) linear stability tongue (T_sync = 22.18 min, kappa_eff = 0.0623 min^-1 at tau_c = 20.5 min vs -0.0353 min^-1 at tau_c = 11.0 min) | Advected 24 x 12 AP x lateral nearest-neighbour delayed Kuramoto PSM lattice (open AP, periodic lateral, per-column period-scaled delay) under a tailbud-anchored exponential FGF8/Wnt frequency profile (f_A = 0.5): N_w = 1.58 kinematic waves (analytic 1.61), anterior wavelength 2.21 S (analytic 2.00 S), N_w monotone in f_A (2.52 -> -0.03 for f_A 0.3 -> 1.0) | Mib1-gated coupling kappa(t) = kappa_max u(t) g(t) with ubiquitination ODE (k_ub = 0.08, k_endo = 0.02 min^-1, u_ss^WT = 0.8) and gamma-secretase gate with 8-min DAPT clearance; mib1-null late R = 0.28 (ALD 5.8), Mib1 restoration at s = 9 rescues to R = 0.77 (PRP 15.3); dose sweep monotone | Emergent ALD/PRP from R_crit = 0.5 crossings of the half-period-smoothed front lateral order parameter + Delta_n_det = 2.5: 5-seed means ALD = 5.41 / 9.21 / 14.24 (obs 5.4 / 9.6 / 14.4), PRP = 14.86 (obs 14.7), RMSE 0.22 somites, Pearson r = 0.9998 (0.9986 over the 4 perturbed regimes); somite stage clock-counted at Omega(kappa(t)) so continuous DAPT lengthens the period from 22.18 to 25.00 min | Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak segmentation on the vendored SEM (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry ratio 0.9606, fitted-sinusoid r = 0.563); transfer_boundary: The frequency profile is a single exponential with f_A = 0.5 and L = 6 S chosen to land in the 1-2-wave range reported for zebrafish; it is not digitised from Morelli (2009) Fig. 3 or Soroldoni (2014) kymographs, and the N_w measurement's reference value is the model's own analytic law | tau_c(x) omega(x) = const (coupling delay scales with the local period) is this script's assumption; the Eulerian-delay alternative was not simulated | k_ub, k_endo, tau_wash, DAPT dose/IC50 and Hill n are the script's reduced rate constants; D_phi = 0.003 rad^2/min, sigma_omega = 0.014 rad/min and tau_wash = 8 min were calibrated so the emergent ALD/PRP lags match the Riedel-Kruse (2007) data (as the paper fitted its desynchronisation rate) | The SEM specimen is a chick embryo (Wikimedia 'Aves Neural tube and somites in chick embryo'), used as a vertebrate somite-metamere stand-in; no zebrafish her1/deltaC in-situ wave pattern is vendored; does_not_claim: PSM shortening and the Soroldoni (2014) Doppler contribution to the segmentation period, cell division/ingression in the tailbud, 3D cell sorting, explicit Mib1 E3-ligase stoichiometry or measured Delta endocytosis rates, or a boundary profile derived from the phase pattern (chi(s) is a coherence-gated synthetic rendering)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:146-153, 197-200 — the reference JSON (which holds the observed regime table) is hashed but not pinned in EXPECTED_SHA256; pin it and update the digest whenever the table changes, with the change recorded in the README.",
            "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:161-162, 174 and 661-744 — D_phi, sigma_omega and tau_wash are calibrated to the ALD/PRP data the model is validated against. Hold out the PRP and the s_in = 4, 9 regimes from calibration explicitly (fit only on s_in = 0), report in-sample vs out-of-sample errors, and add seed-to-seed sd and n_lat / R_crit / Delta_n_det sensitivity to the validation table.",
            "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:172-176 — Mib1 (k_ub, k_endo) and DAPT (dose/IC50, Hill n, tau_wash) rate constants are unmeasured. Anchor k_endo to a measured Delta endocytosis/turnover half-life and the DAPT gate to a published DAPT IC50 / titration curve, or relabel the mechanism as phenomenological in the measurement names.",
            "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:284-319 and 939 — the FGF8/Wnt profile is a single exponential with f_A = 0.5 and the N_w measurement is referenced to the model's own analytic law. Vendor a digitised frequency/wave profile (Morelli 2009 Fig. 3 or Soroldoni 2014 kymograph: wave number vs PSM position, anterior wave speed) and reference N_w and the anterior wavelength ratio to it.",
            "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:413 and Panel B (L1047) — the period-scaled delay tau_c(x) omega(x) = const is asserted, not tested. Add an --eulerian-delay mode (fixed tau_c, history not advected) and report the anterior coherence loss it predicts, so the assumption is tested rather than declared.",
            "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:523-531 — advection is a discrete one-column shift with a fixed PSM length of 6 S and tailbud seeding by copying the last column; model PSM shortening (Soroldoni 2014) so the Doppler contribution to the segmentation period can be computed and compared with the reported period shift.",
            "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:590-604 and 1254-1255 — the somite boundary ribbon chi(s) is a synthetic sin^2 / salt-and-pepper rendering gated by coherence. Derive boundaries from the phase field at the front (e.g. the posterior edge of the cells whose phase crosses 0 at the determination stage) so the defective-window morphology is emergent like the ALD/PRP.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/delta_notch_phase_synchrony/zebrafish_psm_synchrony_specimen.jpg (JSON L48, README L60) and 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:838-847 — the only specimen is a chick SEM compared through a fitted sinusoid. Vendor a CC-licensed Danio rerio her1/deltaC in-situ or Her1-YFP live image with visible PSM stripes and compare the simulated kymograph wavelength and stripe count against it." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.865"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary, Pass 3 builder+assessor) + MorphoEval Dual-Rubric Assessor" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

